**Definition 5.2 (past predicates).** All decoders parse and exhaust the
full binding, require the expected source/code/layout identity and
$|h_k|=k$, and compare $\theta$ with their derived endpoint.

In AcquisitionOffset, check $\mu=1$, $w=111U(\ell)0U(t)$ with the
actual payload length, $\kappa=0$, $d_0=a$, $k=a+t$, and
$0\le t\le d_1-a$. The derived prefix must contain the actual acquired
seed and acquisition annotation at $a$ with the manifest anchor's
already existing source/seed facts. Do not require the later main code
capture, cover number or Ready at $d_1$ to exist in this earlier prefix.

In SourceOffset, check $\mu=1$, $w=111U(\ell)1U(m)U(t)$ with exhaustion,
$\kappa=1$, $k=e+t$ and $0\le t\le f-e$. In the derived actual
history require the outer physical entry event for cycle $j$ at
successor tally $e$, as resolved from the acquired SourceEntrySet,
and no earlier qualifying exit for that cycle. At $k<f$ there is no
qualifying exit yet; at $k=f$ require its actual SourceExitSet event at
that successor tally. Check source/old-count/request facts only insofar
as constructed by $k$ by this finite procedure: fold the derived native
history's constructor roles for this entry/cycle; whenever one of its
three request blocks and descriptor has completed, compare its complete
producer-local reference with the corresponding producer-local reference
resolved from $\gamma$ by ARC §§3.3–3.4. For a partially constructed block
compare only its already measured base/physical identity when available;
do not require a completed descriptor. If the corresponding producer
unified row has completed, compare its old ordinal $m$ and producer-local
origin with the resolved unified origin in $\gamma$. Initial source/
seed identity is checked in every case. The acquired delivery copy's
origin, as opposed to its producer-local component, is a current-service
check. These tests are tuple comparisons and the construction-role fold
on the already derived finite history. In particular a not-yet-supplied header,
not-yet-created request origin or not-yet-delivered unified row is not
required at $e$. It supplies no missing input to §4. Later origins and
the truth of the future exit bound are current-service checks.

Mode0 uses CYCLE Definition 7.1's strict-Zero past tests, with GCA's
mode-zero parser and the same separation of later delivery origins.
Its meaning is not enlarged by the general arm. A numeral matching a
source entry inside a represented bank word is never a physical entry:
tests use represented outer version/PC/row effect and cycle annotation.

